Build a single-file recipe box app with theming.

## Core Features

**Recipe Input & Storage**: A form to add recipes by pasting text. Users enter a recipe name or it auto-guesses from the first non-empty line. Tags are comma-separated (e.g., "weeknight, soup, vegetarian"). Recipes save to localStorage automatically. Seed the app on first visit with two starter recipes (One-Pot Tomato Orzo and Lazy Sunday Chicken Soup) so it feels alive.

**Recipe Display**: Cards in a scrollable list showing recipe name, 2-line text preview, and tag chips. Clicking any card opens a modal with the full recipe text, all tags, and a delete button.

**Tag Cloud & Filtering**: Display all tags with recipe counts. Users can click tags to filter (AND logic—selecting "soup" and "weeknight" shows only recipes with both). A search box filters by recipe name, text content, or tags. Show a "Clear" button when filters are active. Display a count line ("3 recipes in the box" or "Showing 2 of 5").

**The Spinner Hero**: A "Spin for Dinner!" button with a 🥘 icon in a prominent hero section. Clicking it picks a random recipe from the filtered list (or all recipes if no filters). The button animates through recipe names with easing-out delays, then reveals the winner in a card with a "peek at the recipe" link and confetti (🧄 🧅 🥕 🌿 🧂 🍅 ✨) falling. The spinner respects active search/tag filters.

**Theme System**: A theme toggle button (🎨 icon) in the top-right corner with a dropdown menu. Five themes available:
- Cozy Kitchen (default): warm terracotta, cream, butter gold, sage green, cocoa brown
- Midnight Snack: dark theme with orange and purple accents
- Herb Garden: green-dominant palette
- Seaside Supper: blue/ocean colors
- Berry Patch: pink/berry colors

Each theme option displays color swatches. Selected theme persists in localStorage. All colors transition smoothly when switching themes. Apply theme before first paint to prevent flash (use a script tag in head).

## Design

Warm, cozy kitchen aesthetic with:
- Serif typography (Georgia) for a handwritten-recipe feel
- Gingham pattern top border (themed colors & cream check)
- Soft shadows and rounded corners
- Two-column layout (input form left, recipe list right; responsive to single column on mobile)
- Paper-like cards with dashed or solid borders

## Technical Details

- Single-file HTML/CSS/JS app (no build step)
- localStorage for persistence (keys: "recipe-box-v1" for recipes, "recipe-box-theme" for theme)
- Vanilla JS (no frameworks)
- Graceful empty states with helpful emoji & text
- Modal overlay with ESC-to-close and click-outside-to-close
- Responsive design for mobile and desktop
- CSS custom properties (variables) for all theme-dependent colors
